# SatQuery — optional local language layer
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and restart the dev server to route query interpretation
# and answer phrasing through an on-device model instead of the built-in
# deterministic interpreter.
#
# Any runtime that exposes an OpenAI-compatible /v1/chat/completions endpoint
# works. Two that do, both fully offline once the model is pulled:
#
#   Ollama      ollama serve                       -> http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1/chat/completions
#   LM Studio   start the local server in the app  -> http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1/chat/completions
#
# Small models are the point here: the language layer never looks at pixels, so
# a 1B-parameter model is doing language and workflow work, not perception.
#   ollama pull llama3.2:1b
#   ollama pull qwen2.5:1.5b
#
# The model classifies intent only. Answer phrasing stays deterministic, because
# a 1B model measurably degraded it -- dropping measurements, inventing a
# "city", and turning "a 9% built-up increase radar does not confirm" into "a 9%
# increase in optical signals". Set SATQUERY_LOCAL_LLM_PHRASING=1 to experiment
# with model-written phrasing, ideally against a larger model.
#
# Leave these unset and the app runs on the deterministic interpreter, which is
# also fully offline and costs nothing to run. The execution trace and Expert
# Mode always report whichever provider actually answered, by name.

SATQUERY_LOCAL_LLM_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1/chat/completions
SATQUERY_LOCAL_LLM_MODEL=llama3.2:1b
SATQUERY_LOCAL_LLM_NAME=Llama 3.2 1B (local)
